-- coa23-part34.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 34 (Overseas companies), ss 1044 to 1059,
-- lines 14666-14866 of ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively, from the text alone.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- WHAT THIS PART IS. Part 34 is mostly a set of powers for the Secretary of State to make regulations about overseas
-- companies (the regulations are not among the sources). A provision that only confers such a power, or says
-- how the regulations are made (negative or affirmative resolution procedure), is inert (machinery, reason 2) and
-- has no rule here. A provision that fixes what the regulations MUST contain, MUST NOT contain, or what a
-- name or branch counts as, is encoded as a decision function (fork F1 of NOTES.md).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer).
--   JUST TRUE   the text says yes to the case.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words: a "means" definition; "if", "only if", "where", "unless";
--               a flat negative ("does not", "must not"). Each such branch carries
--               -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<the quoted words>"
--   NOTHING     the text does not decide: silent, list not closed, includes, undefined term, points outside the
--               text, or limited by its own wording. Each such branch carries -- NOTHING-kind (<why>).
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every top-level name begins with the label of the section it implements. Money and levels are INPUTS.

