§ `Part 34 - Overseas companies`

§§ `s 1044 Overseas companies`

-- src:14669 | In the Companies Acts an “overseas company” means a company incorporated outside the United Kingdom.
@ref s 1044 Overseas companies (src:14669)
GIVEN `incorporated outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1044 the company is an overseas company` MEANS
    IF `incorporated outside the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an “overseas company” means a company incorporated outside the United Kingdom"

-- s 1045 (company contracts and execution of documents) only confers a power to make regulations: inert (reason 2).

§§ `s 1046 Duty to register particulars`

-- src:14678 | (2) The regulations—
-- src:14679 | (a) must, in the case of a company other than a Gibraltar company, require the company to register particulars if the company opens a branch in the United Kingdom, and
-- src:14680 | (b) may, in the case of a Gibraltar company, require the company to register particulars if the company opens a branch in the United Kingdom, and
-- src:14681 | (c) may, in any case, require the registration of particulars in such other circumstances as may be specified.
@ref s 1046(2) Duty to register particulars: what the regulations must or may require (src:14678-14681)
GIVEN `the company is a Gibraltar company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company opens a branch in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1046(2) the regulations must require the company to register particulars` MEANS
    IF `the company opens a branch in the United Kingdom`
    THEN IF `the company is a Gibraltar company`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) may, in the case of a Gibraltar company, require the company to register particulars if the company opens a branch in the United Kingdom"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the company is a Gibraltar company`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) must, in the case of a company other than a Gibraltar company" is a scope limit (ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)), and (b) and (c) only say "may"
