DECLARE `s 1056 what the regulations must require the company to register` IS ONE OF
    `s 1056(a) particulars identifying every person resident in the United Kingdom authorised to accept service of documents on behalf of the company`
    `s 1056(b) a statement that there is no such person`

-- src:14847 | Regulations under section 1046 (overseas companies: duty to register particulars) must require an overseas company to register—
-- src:14848 | (a) particulars identifying every person resident in the United Kingdom authorised to accept service of documents on behalf of the company, or
-- src:14849 | (b) a statement that there is no such person.
@ref s 1056 Requirement to identify persons authorised to accept service of documents (src:14847-14849)
GIVEN `there is a person resident in the United Kingdom authorised to accept service of documents on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 1056 what the regulations must require the company to register`
`s 1056 what the regulations under section 1046 must require the overseas company to register` MEANS
    IF `there is a person resident in the United Kingdom authorised to accept service of documents on behalf of the company`
    THEN `s 1056(a) particulars identifying every person resident in the United Kingdom authorised to accept service of documents on behalf of the company`
    ELSE `s 1056(b) a statement that there is no such person`

